        <h2>Getting to Pidurangala</h2>
        <p>Pidurangala Rock is in Sigiriya village, directly north of the Sigiriya ticket office — about a 200-metre walk or a 3-minute tuk-tuk ride from the main Sigiriya entrance. From Sigiriya village centre, it is around a 10-minute walk or a very short tuk-tuk (LKR 150–200). The elephant warning applies to any walking in this area before dawn — pre-book a tuk-tuk from your guesthouse the night before.</p>
        <p>From Dambulla (the nearest major town), Sigiriya village is about 20km — a 30-minute tuk-tuk or short bus connection from Dambulla junction. From Colombo, the most common route is bus or private transfer to Dambulla (3.5–4 hours), then onward to Sigiriya. From <a href="/places/kandy">Kandy</a>, allow 3–3.5 hours by road via Matale or Kurunegala. Most Cultural Triangle itineraries combine Pidurangala and Sigiriya with <a href="/places/dambulla">Dambulla Cave Temple</a> and <a href="/places/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a> in a 2–3 day loop.</p>

